# Text files are checked out with LF line ends on every system. Windows' Git would otherwise
# turn them into CRLF, and the files built into the programs (uzu's default config, the docs the
# tests read) would differ from the ones on Linux and macOS.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Files for Windows' own tools and for people on Windows: CRLF there (the installer's script and
# the texts it shows and installs).
*.iss text eol=crlf
packaging/windows/*.txt text eol=crlf
# Never text, whatever their bytes look like: a changed byte breaks the VMP signature and the icon.
*.sig binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
